Package: csemGRM
Title: Conditional Standard Errors of Measurement for the Graded Response Model
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("First", "Last",
           email = "corresponding@email.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Implements analytical and bootstrap estimators of the conditional
    standard error of measurement (CSEM) for the Graded Response Model (GRM;
    Samejima, 1969). While marginal reliability summarizes measurement precision
    across the full latent trait continuum, the CSEM varies as a function of
    the latent trait level theta and provides a more informative picture of
    where a scale measures precisely and where it does not. csemGRM computes
    item and test information functions, derives analytical CSEM as the
    reciprocal of the square root of test information, estimates empirical CSEM
    via parametric bootstrap resampling, computes conditional reliability
    coefficients across the theta continuum, and visualizes CSEM profiles with
    confidence bands. Built-in simulated datasets representative of attitude
    and character measurement instruments are included for immediate
    demonstration. The package is applicable to any GRM-based scale development
    and validation context, including educational, psychological, organizational,
    and clinical measurement.
